            <ArticleTitle>An Unusual Cause of Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest Recorded on a Heartrate Monitor.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e130-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.hlc.2016.04.017</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1443-9506(16)30218-9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary vasospasm is an uncommon, but perhaps under-recognised, cause of cardiac arrest. We present a novel case of an exercise-induced out-of-hospital cardiac arrest due to coronary vasospasm, captured on a heartrate monitor, and discuss the management options for this condition.</AbstractText>
